We will start with **direct substitution** (step A):

$\begin{align}
g(\blueD{\pi})&=\dfrac{1+\sin\left(\dfrac{\blueD{\pi}}{2}\right)}{1-\cos(2(\blueD{\pi}))}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{1+1}{1-1}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{2}{0}
\end{align}$

We got $\dfrac{b}{0}$ where $b\neq0$.

This means that $\displaystyle\lim_{x\to \pi}g(x)$ doesn't exist because there is a vertical **asymptote** at that $x$-value (step B).
